## 🧩🔎 PHASE 23 — CUSTOM DECODER ENGINEERING

### ❗🚫 NEVER MODIFY BUILT-IN RULESETS

Use:

```text
/var/ossec/etc/decoders/local_decoder.xml
```

or a dedicated file under:

```text
/var/ossec/etc/decoders/
```

### 🧩 EXAMPLE

```xml
<decoder name="myapp">
  <program_name>^myapp</program_name>
</decoder>

<decoder name="myapp-login">
  <parent>myapp</parent>
  <regex>User '(\w+)' logged from '(\d+.\d+.\d+.\d+)'</regex>
  <order>user,srcip</order>
</decoder>
```

### 🧠 DECODER PURPOSE

```text
Raw Application Log
       ↓
Pre-decoding
       ↓
Custom Decoder
       ↓
Structured Fields
       ↓
Custom Rule
       ↓
Alert
```

🚩 **BEST PRACTICE:** Keep custom decoder files under `/var/ossec/etc/decoders/` instead of modifying the packaged ruleset.

